John Nduka, course writer; Ojeyemi Matthew Olabemiwo, course editor. Industrial Chemical Technology II, CHM415, National Open University of Nigeria, printed 2018. [Authorized complete 136-page text](https://nou.edu.ng/coursewarecontent/CHM415.pdf) · [University catalogue and use conditions](https://nou.edu.ng/ecourseware-faculty-of-sciences/).

Read the whole text alongside the introductory technology material. Its three modules connect synthesis gases, organic feedstocks and process accounts, selected manufacturing families, and environmental questions. Treat it as an orientation, check reaction/balance claims independently, and deepen each family through the complete public courses and industrial references assigned later.

The institution supplies educational reading/download access with noncommercial educational limitations, not unrestricted reuse. Bibliographic identity, printed year, contents, and full-text availability were checked on 29 October 2026. Catalogue names/codes can vary between programme revisions; this reference identifies the actual CHM415 PDF. No textbook, embedded image, or external exercise media is bundled.

